{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 930,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suppose you're stuck on a desert island with\nno internet, no books, and an evil genius"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4770,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who will only let you off if you can tell\nhim how much a million dollars weighs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8280,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Luckily, you're a physicist, so you can weigh\na million dollars with your mind!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12290,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's how it goes: we approximate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14750,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don't know how much a dollar weighs, but\nwe do know how big it is… more or less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18620,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A dollar is about 15 cm long and 5 cm wide…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21960,
    "dDurationMs": 1489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now how thick is it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23449,
    "dDurationMs": 3551,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don't know that either, but money is made\nout of paper, and we do know that those 'Harry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27000,
    "dDurationMs": 4359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Potter' books were around 800 pages long,\nor 400 sheets of paper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31359,
    "dDurationMs": 2141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I think they were about 5 cm thick…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33500,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that gives 80 sheets per cm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35620,
    "dDurationMs": 4821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we can find the volume of a dollar: 15\ncm long times 5cm wide times one 80th of a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40441,
    "dDurationMs": 3879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cm high is 0.9 cubic centimeters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44320,
    "dDurationMs": 2290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We still don't know how much paper weighs,\nthough."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46610,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we do know that a cubic centimeter of\nwater weighs a gram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49760,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And money's a liquid asset, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50960,
    "dDurationMs": 3439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we'll say a cubic centimeter of dollars\nweighs a gram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54399,
    "dDurationMs": 2891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Multiply 0.9 by a million and we're done!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57290,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A million dollars weighs 900 kilograms, or\ntwo thousand pounds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61330,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why are approximations important in physics?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63680,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, you don't want to attempt a two-month\ncalculation without a ballpark estimate of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67500,
    "dDurationMs": 1330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what you're calculating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68830,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And sometimes approximations like ours can\nbe pretty accurate: case in point, according"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72810,
    "dDurationMs": 8790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the US treasury, a million dollars is a\nton of money."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81600,
    "dDurationMs": 6110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Literally."
    } ]
  } ]
}
